---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../config/site.js';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  description="How SmartPet Index makes money, and the structural reason commissions cannot move a ranking."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Disclosure"
    title="Affiliate Disclosure"
    lede={SITE.disclosure}
    crumbs={[{ label: 'About', href: '/about/' }, { label: 'Disclosure' }]}
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        Some links on this site are affiliate links. If you buy through one, the retailer may pay us a
        commission. You pay the same price either way. That is how the site is funded.
      </p>

      <h2>What commissions cannot do</h2>
      <p>
        Rankings on this site are generated from the scored product database. The ranking code filters and
        sorts on scores and specifications — it has no access to commission rates, and there is no manual
        override that lets an editor move a product up a list. If a product ranks first, it is because its
        weighted score is highest under the published method.
      </p>
      <p>
        We also do not accept payment for a review, a placement, or a score. We do not send scores to brands
        before publication, and we do not give a brand the chance to respond to a score before it goes live.
      </p>

      <h2>Free samples</h2>
      <p>
        Where a brand supplies a unit, we say so on that review page. A supplied unit is assessed
        identically to a bought one, and supplying one buys a brand no influence over the score, the
        wording or the ranking.
      </p>

      <h2>Prices</h2>
      <p>
        Prices shown are the list price at the time we last updated the record, and they move constantly.
        Always check the current price at the retailer before buying. Consumable prices used in our
        long-term cost tables are the cheapest genuine source we could find at the time of writing.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        If anything here is unclear, or something on the site reads to you like an advertisement rather
        than an assessment, <a href="/about/contact/">tell us</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .narrow {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  h2 {
    color: var(--blue-700);
    margin-top: 34px;
  }
</style>
